+\section{Parity corrections for the level-3 mixed point}\label{mixed:sec:eisdim}
+
+The source's convergent double-shuffle computation left formal residual
+coordinates. Such a residual describes the chosen relations; it does not
+exclude reductions supplied by other identities. In particular, put
+$C_j=\Imag\Li_j(\rr)$ for even $j$. The two mixed coordinates presented
+as new in the source have the exact reductions
+\begin{align}
+\Real\Li_{4,1}(\rr^2,\rr)
+ &=\frac{2\pi^4\log3}{243}+\frac{2\pi^2\zeta(3)}{27}
+   -\frac{281\zeta(5)}{162},\label{mixed:eq:eis-parity-41}\\
+\Imag\Li_{5,1}(\rr^2,\rr)
+ &=-3C_6+\frac{\pi^2C_4}{6}+\frac{\pi^4C_2}{90}
+   +\frac{\pi^5\log3}{729}.\label{mixed:eq:eis-parity-51}
+\end{align}
+These are proved in the companion article by the inverse-color
+specialization of depth-two parity; the Bernoulli index-one terms cancel
+before the product of the colors is set to one.
+% Companion proof pointer: sections/mixed.tex, thm:inverse-color.
+All right-hand atoms already occur in the stated single-value basket.
+Consequently these two coordinates add no new directions modulo that
+basket. The full formal quotient must be recomputed after these exact
+relations are included; no corrected numerical dimension is asserted.
+
+\begin{remark}[an explicit search audit target]
+The first reduction is equivalently
+\[
+486\Real\Li_{4,1}(\rr^2,\rr)
+ =4\pi^4\log3+36\pi^2\zeta(3)-843\zeta(5).
+\]
+Its integer-relation height, including the target coefficient, is $843$.
+Thus the source's failure to find it below an approximate $10^4$ scale
+cannot be attributed solely to large coefficients. Reproducing the input
+values, basis, dependence handling and stopping rules is needed to explain
+the failed search; without its scripts, a particular cause is not known.
 \end{remark}
 
